h1 class=\"text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-4xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-4 leading-tight tracking-tight\">UAE Holidays 2026: Complete List of Public and Private Sector Dates</h1><div class=\"flex items-center text-sm text-gray-500 gap-4\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><span class=\"font-semibold text-gray-900\">Last Updated:</span><time dateTime=\"2026-01-01T06:59:21Z\">1 January 2026</time></div></div></header><div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto font-sans\"><div class=\"relative w-full aspect-video md:aspect-21/9 rounded-xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm mb-8 bg-gray-100 border border-gray-100\"><img alt=\"UAE 2026 Holidays celebratory header featuring fireworks over the Burj Khalifa and Sheikh Zayed Grand Mosque, with a lantern and dates.\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"fill\" class=\"object-cover\" style=\"position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent\" src=\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/kxdjzy8e/production/f49d76b1000e7d07af8a937b295eda3ea6631824-1200x800.webp\"/><div class=\"absolute top-4 left-4 bg-white/95 backdrop-blur-md px-3 py-2 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-100 text-center min-w-15\"><span class=\"block text-xs font-bold text-red-600 uppercase tracking-wider\">Jan</span><span class=\"block text-xl font-black text-slate-900 leading-none mt-0.5\">1</span></div></div><div class=\"mb-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2 items-center\"><span class=\"inline-flex items-center bg-blue-50 text-blue-700 text-xs font-bold px-3 py-1 rounded-full uppercase tracking-wider border border-blue-100\">UAE What&#x27;s On: Events, Public Holidays &amp; Festivals 2026</span></div><div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 bg-slate-50 p-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/60 mb-8\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-4\"><div class=\"bg-white p-2.5 rounded-xl text-blue-600 shadow-sm border border-gray-100 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-calendar w-5 h-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M8 2v4\"></path><path d=\"M16 2v4\"></path><rect width=\"18\" height=\"18\" x=\"3\" y=\"4\" rx=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M3 10h18\"></path></svg></div><div><h2 class=\"font-bold text-gray-900 text-xs uppercase tracking-wider mb-1\">Date &amp; Time</h2><p class=\"text-gray-900 font-semibold leading-tight\">Thursday, 1 January 2026</p><p class=\"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-1\">Starts at <!-- -->10:30 PM</p></div></div><div class=\"flex items-start gap-4\"><div class=\"bg-white p-2.5 rounded-xl text-red-500 shadow-sm border border-gray-100 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-map-pin w-5 h-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 10c0 4.993-5.539 10.193-7.399 11.799a1 1 0 0 1-1.202 0C9.539 20.193 4 14.993 4 10a8 8 0 0 1 16 0\"></path><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"10\" r=\"3\"></circle></svg></div><div><h3 class=\"font-bold text-gray-900 text-xs uppercase tracking-wider mb-1\">Location</h3><p class=\"font-semibold text-gray-900 leading-tight mb-0.5\">United Arab Emirates</p><p class=\"text-sm text-gray-500 leading-snug\">Dubai, AE</p></div></div></div><article class=\"prose prose-lg prose-headings:text-slate-900 prose-p:text-slate-700 prose-a:text-blue-600 prose-a:font-semibold prose-img:rounded-xl max-w-none\"><div class=\"mb-10 text-xl font-medium text-slate-800 leading-relaxed border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-6 py-1\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">Planning Your Year of Travel</h2><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Planning your year in the Emirates? For expats and residents, the release of the holiday calendar is the signal to start booking flights. Whether you are planning a summer escape to Europe or a winter staycation in Ras Al Khaimah, timing is everything.</p><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">This guide covers the official <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">UAE holidays in 2026</strong>, the famous &quot;Leave Hacks&quot; to double your time off, and—most importantly—<strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">where to travel</strong> during each break.</p><blockquote class=\"border-l-4 border-[#8B5CF6] pl-6 py-4 text-gray-700 pr-6 my-10 bg-[#ECE4FD]/50 italic text-lg rounded-r-lg\">Editor&#x27;s Note: This guide details the predicted holiday calendar for 2026 based on astronomical calculations and the UAE Cabinet&#x27;s standardized holiday framework. Islamic dates are subject to moon sighting.</blockquote></div><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\"><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">At a Glance: UAE Public Holidays 2026</strong></h2><div class=\"my-8\"><div class=\"hidden md:block overflow-hidden border border-gray-400 shadow-sm\"><table class=\"w-full text-base text-left border-collapse\"><thead class=\"bg-[#312e81] text-white\"><tr><th scope=\"col\" class=\"px-3 py-2 font-bold border-r border-indigo-700 last:border-r-0 whitespace-nowrap\">Holiday</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"px-3 py-2 font-bold border-r border-indigo-700 last:border-r-0 whitespace-nowrap\">Official/Predicted Date</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"px-3 py-2 font-bold border-r border-indigo-700 last:border-r-0 whitespace-nowrap\">Days Off</th></tr></thead><tbody class=\"divide-y divide-gray-200 bg-white\"><tr class=\"hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors\"><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 font-bold text-gray-900\">New Year&#x27;s Day</td><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 \">Jan 1 (Thursday)1 Day</td><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 \">1 Day</td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors\"><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 font-bold text-gray-900\">Eid Al Fitr</td><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 \">Mar 20 – Mar 22 (Fri–Sun)*</td><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 \">3–4 Days</td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors\"><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 font-bold text-gray-900\">Arafat Day</td><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 \">May 26 (Tuesday)*</td><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 \">1 Day</td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors\"><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 font-bold text-gray-900\">Eid Al Adha</td><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 \">May 27 – May 29 (Wed–Fri)*</td><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 \">3 Days</td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors\"><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 font-bold text-gray-900\">Islamic New Year</td><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 \">Jun 16 (Tuesday)*</td><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 \">1 Day</td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors\"><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 font-bold text-gray-900\">Prophet&#x27;s Birthday</td><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 \">Aug 25 (Tuesday)*</td><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 \">1 Day</td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors\"><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 font-bold text-gray-900\">National Day</td><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 \">Dec 2 – Dec 3 (Wed–Thu)\t2 D</td><td class=\"px-3 py-4 border-r border-gray-400 last:border-r-0 text-gray-800 \">2 Days</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"md:hidden space-y-6\"><div class=\"bg-white border border-gray-200 border-l-4 border-l-[#8B5CF6] rounded-xl shadow-sm overflow-hidden\"><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col border-b border-gray-100 bg-gray-50\"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Holiday</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed font-black text-gray-900 text-lg\">New Year&#x27;s Day</span></div><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col border-b border-gray-100 \"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Official/Predicted Date</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-800\">Jan 1 (Thursday)1 Day</span></div><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col  \"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Days Off</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-800\">1 Day</span></div></div><div class=\"bg-white border border-gray-200 border-l-4 border-l-[#8B5CF6] rounded-xl shadow-sm overflow-hidden\"><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col border-b border-gray-100 bg-gray-50\"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Holiday</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed font-black text-gray-900 text-lg\">Eid Al Fitr</span></div><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col border-b border-gray-100 \"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Official/Predicted Date</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-800\">Mar 20 – Mar 22 (Fri–Sun)*</span></div><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col  \"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Days Off</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-800\">3–4 Days</span></div></div><div class=\"bg-white border border-gray-200 border-l-4 border-l-[#8B5CF6] rounded-xl shadow-sm overflow-hidden\"><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col border-b border-gray-100 bg-gray-50\"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Holiday</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed font-black text-gray-900 text-lg\">Arafat Day</span></div><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col border-b border-gray-100 \"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Official/Predicted Date</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-800\">May 26 (Tuesday)*</span></div><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col  \"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Days Off</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-800\">1 Day</span></div></div><div class=\"bg-white border border-gray-200 border-l-4 border-l-[#8B5CF6] rounded-xl shadow-sm overflow-hidden\"><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col border-b border-gray-100 bg-gray-50\"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Holiday</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed font-black text-gray-900 text-lg\">Eid Al Adha</span></div><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col border-b border-gray-100 \"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Official/Predicted Date</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-800\">May 27 – May 29 (Wed–Fri)*</span></div><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col  \"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Days Off</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-800\">3 Days</span></div></div><div class=\"bg-white border border-gray-200 border-l-4 border-l-[#8B5CF6] rounded-xl shadow-sm overflow-hidden\"><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col border-b border-gray-100 bg-gray-50\"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Holiday</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed font-black text-gray-900 text-lg\">Islamic New Year</span></div><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col border-b border-gray-100 \"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Official/Predicted Date</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-800\">Jun 16 (Tuesday)*</span></div><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col  \"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Days Off</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-800\">1 Day</span></div></div><div class=\"bg-white border border-gray-200 border-l-4 border-l-[#8B5CF6] rounded-xl shadow-sm overflow-hidden\"><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col border-b border-gray-100 bg-gray-50\"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Holiday</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed font-black text-gray-900 text-lg\">Prophet&#x27;s Birthday</span></div><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col border-b border-gray-100 \"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Official/Predicted Date</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-800\">Aug 25 (Tuesday)*</span></div><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col  \"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Days Off</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-800\">1 Day</span></div></div><div class=\"bg-white border border-gray-200 border-l-4 border-l-[#8B5CF6] rounded-xl shadow-sm overflow-hidden\"><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col border-b border-gray-100 bg-gray-50\"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Holiday</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed font-black text-gray-900 text-lg\">National Day</span></div><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col border-b border-gray-100 \"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Official/Predicted Date</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-800\">Dec 2 – Dec 3 (Wed–Thu)\t2 D</span></div><div class=\"px-5 py-5 flex flex-col  \"><span class=\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-600 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2\">Days Off</span><span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-800\">2 Days</span></div></div></div></div><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\"><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Note:</strong> Dates marked with (*) are subject to moon sighting and official government confirmation.</p><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">The 2026 Travel Planner: Where to Go &amp; When</h2><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Maximizing your holidays isn&#x27;t just about the dates; it&#x27;s about matching the destination to the season. Here is your roadmap for the year.</p><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">1. The Spring Break: Eid Al-Fitr (March 20–22)</h3><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">The Vibe:</strong> The &quot;Sweet Spot.&quot; It is not too hot in the GCC yet, making it perfect for regional travel.</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">International:</strong> <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Oman</strong> (Salalah or Muscat), <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Azerbaijan</strong> (Baku), or <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Georgia</strong> (Tbilisi). These are short flights (3-4 hours) and offer cool, green escapes without a long haul.</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Local Staycation:</strong> This is the ideal time for a <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Desert Safari</strong> or glamping trip before the summer heat kicks in. Head to <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Al Qudra Lakes</strong> or the <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Liwa Desert</strong> for a starlit night.</li></ul><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">2. The Summer Escape: Eid Al-Adha (May 26–30)</h3><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">The Vibe:</strong> The UAE heat is rising. It is time to leave the desert or head to high altitudes.</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">International:</strong> With a potential <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">9-day break</strong> (see hack below), aim for <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Europe</strong> (Italy, Switzerland) or the <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">USA</strong>. The Mediterranean weather is flawless in late May—warm enough for swimming but without the August crowds.</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Local Staycation:</strong> Escape the humidity by heading to the mountains. <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Jebel Jais</strong> in Ras Al Khaimah offers temperatures 10°C cooler than the city, perfect for ziplining and hiking.</li></ul><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">3. The Winter Celebration: National Day (Dec 2–3)</h3><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">The Vibe:</strong> The UAE is officially the best place on Earth in December.</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">International:</strong> Most residents stay put to enjoy the local festivities, but if you must fly, <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Thailand</strong> or the <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Maldives</strong> offer great winter sun.</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Local Staycation:</strong> Head to <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Hatta</strong> for kayaking, <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Khorfakkan</strong> for camping, or book a luxury beach resort on <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Palm Jumeirah</strong>. The entire country turns into a festival with parades, air shows, and fireworks over the <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Burj Khalifa</strong>.</li></ul><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">The &quot;Leave Hack&quot;: Turn 12 Holidays into 38 Days Off</h2><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Want that trip to the USA or Japan? You need more than 3 days. Here is the secret formula for 2026:</p><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\"><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">1. The Eid Al-Adha Mega Break (9 Days Off)</strong></h3><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">The Holiday:</strong> Arafat Day &amp; Eid fall from <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Tuesday, May 26</strong> to <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Friday, May 29</strong>.</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">The Hack:</strong> Take <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Monday, May 25</strong> as annual leave.</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">The Result:</strong> You get a continuous break from <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Saturday, May 23</strong> to <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Saturday, May 30</strong>.</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Total Off:</strong> 9 Days (using only 1 leave day).</li></ul><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\"><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">2. The National Day Finale (9 Days Off)</strong></h3><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">The holiday:</strong> Commemoration Day &amp; National Day likely covers <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Tuesday, Dec 1</strong> to <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Thursday, Dec 3</strong>.</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">The Hack:</strong> Take <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Monday, Nov 3,0,</strong> and <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Friday, Dec 4,</strong> as annual leave.</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">The Result:</strong> You bridge the previous weekend (Nov 28-29) with the next weekend (Dec 5-6).</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Total Off:</strong> 9 Days (using only 2 leave days).</li></ul><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">3. School Holidays in UAE 2026</h2><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">For parents planning family vacations, aligning with the school calendar is critical. Here are the official dates from the Ministry of Education for the 2025–2026 academic year:</p><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Spring Break:</strong> March 16 – March 29, 2026.<ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li><em>Note:</em> This break coincides with the predicted dates for <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Eid Al Fitr</strong> (March 20–22), allowing for an extended family celebration without missing school days.</li></ul></li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Summer Break:</strong> Starts July 6, 2026.<ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li><em>Note:</em> The last official day of school for students is <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">July 3, 2026</strong> (Friday).</li></ul></li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Winter Break (2026/2027):</strong> Expected to start mid-December 2026 (Dates TBC).</li></ul><hr class=\"w-full my-6 border-t border-gray-200\"/><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">Smart Travel Tips for UAE Expats</h2><ol class=\"list-decimal ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary font-medium text-lg\"><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Visa-Free Options:</strong> For last-minute plans, UAE residents can often visit <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Georgia, Azerbaijan, the Maldives, and the Seychelles</strong> with visa-on-arrival or e-visas.</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Schengen Visas:</strong> If planning for Europe during the Eid Al Adha break (May), apply for your Schengen visa in <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">January</strong>. Appointment slots in Dubai/Abu Dhabi are known to fill up 3-4 months in advance.</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Flight Prices:</strong> Always book &quot;refundable&quot; or &quot;flexible&quot; tickets for Islamic holidays. If the moon sighting shifts the date by 24 hours, you want the ability to change your flight without a penalty.</li></ol><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\"><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Important Considerations</strong></h3><ol class=\"list-decimal ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary font-medium text-lg\"><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Moon Sighting is Final:</strong> All Islamic dates are predictions. Do not book non-refundable flights for the exact days; give yourself a +/- 1-day buffer.</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">School Holidays:</strong> Spring break for most UAE schools is expected to align with the Eid Al-Fitr period in late March, making it the busiest travel week of Q1.</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Sector Differences:</strong> While the UAE government typically unifies public and private sector holidays, the number of granted days can sometimes vary. Always confirm specific dates with your employer&#x27;s HR policy.</li></ol></article><div class=\"mt-16 pt-10 border-t border-gray-100\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 flex items-center gap-2\">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class=\"bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm overflow-hidden mb-12\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 border-b border-gray-100 bg-gray-50/50\"><h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 flex items-center gap-3\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-circle-question-mark w-6 h-6 text-primary\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"></circle><path d=\"M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3\"></path><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"></path></svg>Frequently Asked Questions</h2></div><div class=\"divide-y divide-gray-100\"><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">When is the next long weekend in UAE 2026?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">After New Year&#x27;s Day, the next major long weekend is Eid Al Fitr, expected around March 20, 2026.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">How many days off for Eid Al Adha 2026?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Residents can expect a 6-day break, starting from Arafat Day (likely May 26) through the weekend.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">What is the longest holidays for travel in 2026?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Eid Al-Adha (May) offers the best opportunity for long-haul travel. With just one day of annual leave, you can unlock a 9-day vacation, making it viable to travel to the USA, Japan, or Australia.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">Are public and private sector holidays the same in UAE?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Yes. The UAE Cabinet has unified the number of official holidays for both public and private sectors.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">Can I travel during Ramadan 2026?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Yes. Ramadan 2026 will be in Feb/March. Travel is often cheaper during the Holy Month before the Eid rush begins, though some services in Muslim countries may be reduced during daylight hours.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">How many public holidays are there in the UAE in 2026?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">There are <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">7 official public holiday occasions</strong> in 2026 sanctioned by the UAE Cabinet. These include New Year&#x27;s Day, Eid Al Fitr, Arafat Day, Eid Al Adha, Islamic New Year, the Prophet&#x27;s Birthday, and National Day. In total, residents can expect approximately <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">13 days of public holidays</strong> throughout the year.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">How many days off for Eid Al Fitr 2026?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Residents can typically expect a break of <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">3 to 4 days</strong> for Eid Al Fitr. In 2026, the holiday is predicted to fall from <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Friday, March 20, to Sunday, March 22</strong>. Since the holiday spans Ramadan 29 to Shawwal 3, the exact duration depends on the moon sighting, but it will likely create a long weekend.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">How to get more holidays in 2026?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">You can maximize your time off by &quot;bridging&quot; public holidays with your annual leave. For example, during <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Eid Al Adha in May</strong>, the holiday falls from Tuesday to Friday. By booking just <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">one day off (Monday, May 25)</strong>, you can connect the previous weekend and enjoy a massive <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">9-day vacation</strong> while using only a single day of your annual leave balance.</p></div></details></div></div></div></div></main><aside class=\"w-full lg:w-80 shrink-0 space-y-8 mt-12 lg:mt-0\"><div class=\"bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm relative overflow-hidden\"><div class=\"absolute top-0 right-0 w-24 h-24 bg-primary/5 rounded-full translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2\"></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-4 mb-4 relative z-10\"><div class=\"w-14 h-14 bg-gray-50 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center overflow-hidden border-2 border-white shadow-md\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-shield-check w-7 h-7 text-[#4b0082]\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 13c0 5-3.5 7.5-7.66 8.95a1 1 0 0 1-.67-.01C7.5 20.5 4 18 4 13V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1c2 0 4.5-1.2 6.24-2.72a1.17 1.17 0 0 1 1.52 0C14.51 3.81 17 5 19 5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1z\"></path><path d=\"m9 12 2 2 4-4\"></path></svg></div><div><h3 class=\"font-bold text-gray-900 leading-tight\">Editorial Team</h3><p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 font-medium uppercase tracking-wider\">Expert Reviewers</p></div></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4 relative z-10\">We research, test, and review the best products in the UAE so you don&#x27;t have to.<span class=\"font-semibold text-gray-900\"> Unbiased &amp; Independent.</span></p></div><div class=\"bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm lg:sticky lg:top-24\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2 mb-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-trending